1. How well we fine tune our RAG to produce better result or generate
better result is called "Harness"

Agent ---> System we develop that communicates with LLM to produce the result
or to act according to the user prompt

Agent = Model + Harness

What a harness actually contains

A production-grade harness contains five layers:

1. tool orchestration,
2. verification loops,
3. context and memory,
4. guardrails
5. observability.

Which tools the agent is allowed to call, and when
Checking/validating the model's proposed actions before executing them (schemas, permissions, budgets)
Logging and monitoring what the agent actually did
Capturing failures and feeding corrections back in so the same mistake doesn't repeat
Managing memory/context across long or multi-day tasks